1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,689
CHAPTER 4 — THE BET NOBODY WANTED

2
00:00:04,039 --> 00:00:13,654
In 2006, Huang made an unusual bet. It was called CUDA, and it allowed graphics cards to be used for any calculation, not just games.

3
00:00:13,874 --> 00:00:21,643
Scientists and programmers could put those thousands of hands to work on whatever they wanted: physics, weather, medicine.

4
00:00:21,863 --> 00:00:27,325
Wall Street didn't like it. It cost a fortune, and nobody could see how it would make money.

5
00:00:27,545 --> 00:00:33,622
For years, the company was worth around ten billion dollars, and barely moved.

6
00:00:34,472 --> 00:00:37,933
It was a bridge toward a city that didn't exist yet.
